ars clinically concerning, biopsy rather than watchful waiting; often excisional biopsy is preferred for a suspicious pigmented lesion\n- Short-interval monitoring alone would usually not be the first choice if melanoma is a meaningful concern\n\nBottom line: in this synthetic scenario, the combination of ABCDE-type warning signs and documented change makes melanoma an important rule-out, so expedited dermatology assessment would typically be recommended. If you want, I can also format this as a clean “expected SLM dermatology output” for testing.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_00d963f4f2b36c610169d641caf7948191927209f60822ff4e\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":442,"output":458,"cacheRead":9856,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":10756,"cost":{"input":0.001105,"output":0.00687,"cacheRead":0.002464,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.010439}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775649220773}}
